# DustMultiSite regression test — Phase 20 multi-mine PHREEQC tables.
#
# Two named mine sites with non-overlapping bounding boxes.
# Domain: 3000x3000 m, 8x8 cells -> dx=375 m.
# Cell centres: x in {187.5, 562.5, ..., 2812.5}, y in {187.5, ..., 2812.5}.
#
# Site 1: "mine_north" x=[0,3000] y=[1500,3000]
#   -> cells (i,j) where y_c > 1500: j in {4,5,6,7} = 32 cells.
# Site 2: "mine_south" x=[0,3000] y=[0,1500]
#   -> cells (i,j) where y_c < 1500: j in {0,1,2,3} = 32 cells.
# No overlap; all 64 cells assigned (0 unassigned).
#
# site_phreeqc_files are empty strings -> PHREEQC factor = 1.0 (no reduction).
# With factor=1.0: Phase 5 u*_t is unchanged by Phase 20 (same as single-site).
#
# Expected results:
#   (1) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 20: 2 mine sites registered.
#   (2) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 20: unassigned cells = 0.
#   (3) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 20: site 1 cells=32, site 2 cells=32.
#   (4) dust_site_id MultiFab: cells j>=4 have value 1.0,
#       cells j<4 have value 2.0, no cells have value 0.0.
#   (5) With empty PHREEQC files: u*_t unchanged vs single-site run.
#   (6) plt_dust_00005 contains 20 variables including dust_site_id.
#   (7) DustMetadata.json n_variables=20.
#   (8) [DUST DEBUG] advance shows site_id_max=2 each step.
#   (9) Run exits code 0.
#
# To test PHREEQC reduction: provide real PHREEQC file paths and verify
# that u*_t differs between site 1 and site 2 cells.
# To test overlap: set site 2 bbox to cover the whole domain; all cells
# should be assigned site 2 (last-wins rule).
#
# References:
#   Parkhurst & Appelo (2013). PHREEQC Version 3.
#     https://pubs.usgs.gov/tm/06/a43/
#   Marticorena & Bergametti (1995). J. Geophys. Res., 100, 16415.
#     https://doi.org/10.1029/95JD00690
#   Shao & Lu (2000). J. Geophys. Res., 105, 22437.
#     https://doi.org/10.1029/2000JD900304
#   ERF_FireGrid.H (spatial metadata pattern):
#     https://github.com/hgopalan/ERF/blob/ERF-Fire/Source/Fire/ERF_FireGrid.H

